**The script's source audit under-reports.** It scans only the structural slots, so it returns 0 untagged. Independent scan of the body found four untagged load-bearing quotes it never reaches — including DiCaprio's "She was the fabric of this movie," which has no outlet, no date, and no THR entry in `citations`, and which is reproduced verbatim in FAQ 2. That's the line an AI answer engine lifts, sourced to nothing. Same for Taylor's "You were chosen for a reason," an entirely unattributed "I remember being very nervous that day," and the Best Picture stage pair. Since editor comments are stripped on push, the Testimony Ledger doesn't cover any of them.

